# Contract sync tests compare raw bytes, and the generators emit an LF banner
# followed by source text. Under core.autocrlf=true, a CRLF checkout of the
# LF-stored contract files is one byte longer than the derived output, which
# makes the contract-sync suites fail. docs/derive_deepseek.gd embeds its
# harness section as a literal string, so a CRLF checkout of that script also
# injects CRLF into the derived DEEPSEEK.md. Force LF for the trio plus the
# generator scripts so a fresh checkout matches what make_agents.gd and
# make_deepseek.gd derive.
AGENTS.md text eol=lf
CLAUDE.md text eol=lf
DEEPSEEK.md text eol=lf
docs/*.gd text eol=lf

# ADR-041 (Sprint 16, art asset integration): Godot always writes .import
# sidecars and .uid files with LF, regardless of platform. Under
# core.autocrlf=true a checkout gives them CRLF, so every independent
# worktree's own `--headless --import` run immediately "modifies" every
# tracked sidecar back to LF - three parallel workstream agents each hit
# this and correctly declined to stage the resulting churn. Force LF so a
# fresh checkout already matches what Godot writes and re-importing is a
# no-op diff.
*.import text eol=lf
*.uid text eol=lf
